4:   "summary": "Integration review. Changed files: NONE. I made no edits to platform/ or web/ because I found no defect that needs one.\n\nWhat I did: I read loop/acceptance.md, platform/README.md, the build-03 tester handoff, and the five verification result.json files (build-02, build-03, wad-01, input-01, rendering-01). I did not open web/, platform/ source, the tests, or the other handoffs or process.json files, so this is not a full source review.\n\nWhat I could not do: I have no execution tool, so I did NOT run the protected acceptance checks (tests/test_browser.py, tests/browser.mjs, tests/test_audio.py, tests/test_loop.py) in this invocation.\n\nEvidence from earlier tester runs, which I only read:\n- All five verification results report status PASS at source digest 6ef3e2af1bf51ab5ffc051b67b311a2a3e889da805d322913d19fe02deb9af12. That is the digest I was given for this task.\n- In each, the build command exited 0 (about 4-5s) and the tests command exited 0 (about 20s).\n- This covers the automated scope only. test_loop.py is not shown in these results.\n\nRemaining defects and risks (none confirmed as defects):\n- The verification results record only return codes and timings. The Emscripten 4.0.18 version is inferred from the successful build, not confirmed.\n- The 4-5s build time is short for a full compile. It is unexplained and may be a cached or incremental build.\n- build.sh passes -w, which hides compiler warnings. That script is protected, so this is a human-owned item.\n\nNot covered by the automated checks (NOT ESTABLISHED, per loop/acceptance.md):\n- Actual door and switch activation.\n- OS focus transitions.\n- Physical speakers and musical fidelity.\n- Save persistence across reloads.\n- Mouse aiming. The engine's mouse event generation is commented out in i_input.c.\n- A manual playthrough was not performed by me. It is separate human evidence and must not be invented.\n\nSystem-evaluation and full-capstone requirements not established:\n- Actual autonomous repair of two blind regressions.\n- Live resumption.\n- Accountability.\n- Design rationale and reflection.\n- The teammate exercise is NOT PERFORMED, at the user's explicit request.\n- Historical token and cost usage is unknown.\n- tests/test_loop.py uses fixtures and is not evidence of real repair or resumption.\n\nEvidence needed next: a fresh tester run of the fixed verification at digest 6ef3e2af... with a raw build log and `emcc --version`, a manual gameplay record by a human, and the human-owned write-ups. DONE means this was handed off, not accepted. This is a scoped automated result, not full assignment acceptance.",
